# Multi-MCU AVR fan-out validation
#
# Exercises the EMULATOR multi-bridge plumbing introduced in this PR
# (one simavr bridge per dict, klippy reactor connects to a `:`-list
# of tick sockets and broadcasts advance/done in lockstep). All three
# MCUs are atmega2560 -- the goal is to validate the fan-out path
# itself, not any cross-architecture work. sample-multi-mcu.cfg has
# the main mcu driving X/Y, zboard driving Z, and auxboard running
# the extruder heater + bed heater + fan + thermistors.
DICTIONARY atmega2560.dict other=atmega2560.dict
CONFIG multi_mcu_avr.cfg
EMULATOR multi_mcu_avr.fixture.json

# A few harmless gcode lines to get past klippy:ready and exercise
# motion / heater paths.
G28
M114
M105

# Each MCU loaded successfully (klippy logs one "Loaded MCU 'name'"
# per MCU it identifies on startup).
EXPECT_LOG_CONTAINS "Loaded MCU 'mcu'"
EXPECT_LOG_CONTAINS "Loaded MCU 'other'"
EXPECT_LOG_NOT_CONTAINS "Internal error"
